name: signal-definition
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: |
  Fires when a commit gives an orphaned auto-registered signal its
  definition — the worldmodel mints a `<name>.signal` stub the moment
  a commit message declares a signal name with no file, and this
  signal marks the commit that refines the stub into a real note.

  Witnessed 2026-10-23: the KORU127 registry drain declared
  `Signal: registry-drift` before a definition existed; the gate
  minted the orphan, and the follow-up commit wrote the note.
route: surface
